Why This Is Asked
- Tests end-to-end Azure data engineering: ingestion, governance, lineage, schema drift, and disaster recovery.

Key Concepts
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, Delta Live Tables, Azure Schema Registry, Purview, Event Hubs, SFTP ingestion, cross-region DR, backfill with time travel, data quality gates.

Code Example
```javascript
// High-level pseudo-setup for DLT-like pipeline (language tag as required)
const domainContract = fetchSchemaFromRegistry('telemetry');
const stream = readFromEventHub('telemetry');
const batch = readFromSFTP('/daily/transactions.csv');
const enriched = stream.union(batch).transform(/* drift-tolerant logic */);
writeDeltaLake(enriched, '/lake/telemetry');
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement cross-domain schema evolution without breaking downstream consumers?
- How would you validate lineage completeness across streaming and batch paths in Purview?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates the ability to design a comprehensive lakehouse architecture that seamlessly integrates streaming and batch data ingestion while maintaining data quality, governance, and disaster recovery capabilities within the Azure ecosystem.

## Key Concepts

- Delta Live Tables for automated ETL with incremental processing
- Schema drift management through auto-evolution capabilities
- Structured streaming integration from Azure Event Hubs
- Batch data ingestion from SFTP sources
- Data quality enforcement using Delta Live Tables Expectations
- PII protection through custom UDFs and governance controls
- End-to-end lineage tracking with Azure Purview integration
- Cross-region disaster recovery using ADLS Gen2 geo-replication
- Backfill strategies with dedicated pipeline runs

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII masking implementation
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).*(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{4})/, '$1****$2');
  return r;
}
```
